  "notes": "Almarai Co. — Saudi Arabia's largest dairy and food group, listed on Tadawul. Calendar fiscal year (Dec 31). Reportable IFRS 8 segments: Dairy and Juices, Bakery, Poultry, Farming (alfalfa/fodder + Argentine Fondomonte farmland holdings). Farmland exposure is via the Farming segment — Almarai owns ~50,000 ha of farmland in Argentina (Fondomonte, ~123k acres) plus alfalfa farms in Saudi Arabia, USA (Fondomonte California / Arizona). Most revenue is dairy/food (>85%); farmland is strategic feedstock supply. Quarterly figures from Tadawul Form 8 quarterly disclosures and Almarai IR press releases; annual data from 2020-2024 annual reports. Acres figure is Argentine Fondomonte holdings only (~50,000 ha × 2.47 ÷ 1000 = 123.5k acres); excludes leased Saudi/US fodder farms. Net debt = total borrowings − cash & cash equivalents. Property book = property, plant & equipment + biological assets. Some segment splits estimated from disclosed annual breakdowns. Pre-2020 annual data (FY2005-FY2019) compiled from Almarai IR archive (annual reports + Tadawul disclosures since the IPO in July 2005). Pre-2009 was dairy + juices only (Western Bakeries acquired Dec 2007 — bakery contribution from FY2008; Hail Agricultural (HADCO/poultry) acquired Aug 2009 — poultry segment from FY2010; Argentine Fondomonte farmland acquired in 2011 and Fondomonte California/Arizona in 2014). Accordingly totalAcresK ramps from 0 in FY2005-2010 to ~50k ha (~124k acres) by FY2014 onward; revenueBySegmentMM only meaningful from FY2010 once all four segments existed.",
